+# Native Weather Preview
+
+Run from the BizReader checkout:
+
+```sh
+python build/weather-display-web/tests/preview/render.py weather.pgm
+```
+
+This compiles the current sketch's display functions mechanically, without
+copying a separate layout. `host.hpp` supplies Arduino and hardware stubs. Text
+uses the same compressed glyphs and bounds calculation as LilyGo's font driver,
+with native zlib decompression. The primitive host rasterizer can differ by a
+pixel from the embedded rasterizer. It does not test panel refresh or hardware.
+
+AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer are enabled. The fixture has no
+credentials and never connects to a network or serial port. Output is a 960x540
+PGM. The executable reports final ink bounds and dark pixel attempts outside the
+safe rectangle `(28, 28)` through `(931, 511)`, exiting nonzero for violations.
+The actual `UpdateLocalTime` routine also executes against a fixed UTC clock,
+checking the real Vietnamese weekday and lunar-date strings and their glyphs.
+
+Override the current and forecast icon or weather description for edge cases:
+
+```sh
+PREVIEW_ICON=11n PREVIEW_DESCRIPTION='thunderstorm with heavy rain' \
+  python build/weather-display-web/tests/preview/render.py storm.pgm
+```
+
+After compilation, exercise all 18 standard day/night icon variants:
+
+```sh
+python build/weather-display-web/tests/preview/check_cases.py
+```
+
+Set `PREVIEW_EPOCH` to test another date. These checks measure screen edges, not
+semantic content overlap; inspect the generated PGM/PNG visually too.
+
+`generated.inc` and `weather-preview` are regenerated each run. They contain
+display code only, not the private Wi-Fi or OpenWeather configuration.
+
+## Calendar Dashboard
+
+The minute-clock dashboard has a separate harness, so hardware RTC, radio and
+sleep routines never run on the host:
+
+```sh
+python build/weather-display-web/tests/preview/render_dashboard.py
+python build/weather-display-web/tests/preview/check_dashboard_cases.py
+```
+
+`render_dashboard.py` includes the actual `weather_dashboard.h` and extracts the
+current sketch's real vendor icon and drawing routines. It uses the generated
+Vietnamese fonts directly. The cases cover every day/night icon, missing data,
+stale forecasts, failed requests, long location names, cold weather, six-row
+months, leap dates and year boundaries. The clock-only case verifies that
+changing the minute modifies no pixel outside `(690, 28, 240, 78)`. All cases
+check the 28-pixel physical bezel margin and run with ASan/UBSan enabled.
+
+These checks do not prove the real panel's refresh quality or battery life.
